  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">01</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Rationalize Heavy-Discount SKUs</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Products in the 80–100% discount bracket average the lowest ratings (4.02★) and lowest review volume (9,954 avg). These likely represent clearance inventory or low-quality private label. Audit this cohort of 96 products and remove or restructure rather than continuing to promote them at extreme discounts.</div>
      <span class="rec-stat">80–100% disc. bracket: 4.02★ avg vs. 4.21★ for 0–10% disc.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">02</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Grow the Premium Segment (₹5K+)</div>
      <div class="rec-body">The ₹5K+ price segment delivers the highest average rating (4.17★) with the smallest average discount (33.5%), suggesting these products earn customer satisfaction on merit, not price cuts. Prioritize assortment expansion in this segment — increasing premium SKU share improves catalog quality scores without margin erosion.</div>
      <span class="rec-stat">₹5K+ segment: 4.17★ avg, 33.5% avg discount (206 products)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">03</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Elevate Home &amp; Kitchen Category</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Home &amp; Kitchen ranks last among the three major categories with a 4.04★ average across 448 products, despite only 40% average discounting (lowest intensity). The lower ratings are not discount-related, pointing to underlying product or listing quality issues. Invest in content quality reviews, stricter supplier ratings thresholds, and sub-category curation for this segment.</div>
      <span class="rec-stat">Home &amp; Kitchen: 4.04★ vs. catalog avg 4.10★ across 448 products</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">04</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Leverage Office Products as a Quality Benchmark</div>
      <div class="rec-body">Office Products achieves the highest average rating (4.31★) with the lowest average discount intensity (12.4%) — a clear signal that this category succeeds through product quality, not promotions. Use Office Products' supplier and content standards as a quality benchmark for other categories, and consider expanding assortment to capitalize on high customer satisfaction.</div>
      <span class="rec-stat">Office Products: 4.31★, only 12.4% avg discount (31 products)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <div class="rec-num">05</div>
      <div class="rec-title">Prioritize High-Engagement SKU Quality Control</div>
      <div class="rec-body">The top 10 most-reviewed products (all Electronics, avg 363K+ reviews) set catalog perception for millions of customers. All rate 4.1–4.4★ — healthy but not exceptional. A single quality failure in these SKUs has outsized reputational impact. Implement proactive monitoring and faster listing remediation for products exceeding 100K reviews.</div>
      <span class="rec-stat">Top 10 products avg 380K+ reviews each; median product: 5,179</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</div><!-- /container -->

